1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,090
Questions in Hindi and English, side by side…

2
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:06,620
a diagram straight from the paper…

3
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:10,670
chemistry structures… and full JEE-level maths.

4
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:15,380
In the next few minutes, you're going to build this entire paper yourself.

5
00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:22,310
Hi!

6
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:29,340
Today we'll take this JEE Main sample paper, and turn selected questions into a complete test on TestoZa.

7
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:32,100
Every question teaches you one new trick.

8
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,350
So, let's get started.

9
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:37,880
In the menu on the left, click Create Test.

10
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:40,460
At the top, type the test name — JEE Main Mini Mock.

11
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:46,110
Just below it, add a one-line description.

12
00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:48,490
Candidates see this before they start.

13
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:48,540
Now pick the time.

14
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:54,880
Tap the three-hour button, and it fills in a hundred and eighty minutes for you.

15
00:00:54,880 --> 00:01:00,700
"Only my students" means the test is visible only to the people you send the link to.

16
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:07,750
In Marking, choose JEE / NEET — plus four for a right answer, and minus one for a wrong one.

17
00:01:07,750 --> 00:01:12,980
And if you open Institution branding, you can add your institute's name and logo too.

18
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:15,770
Now scroll down to Questions.

19
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:17,590
The first one is physics.

20
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:24,840
Let's type it in English first — a stone, a string of length L, and a vertical circle.

21
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:27,880
Now, the same question in Hindi.

22
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:34,530
Above the question, click the button next to English, search for Hindi in the menu, and pick it.

23
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:37,680
Now just type in English letters — e, k…

24
00:01:37,670 --> 00:01:42,420
p, a, t, t, h, a, r — and the moment you press space, each word turns into Hindi.

25
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:47,330
So right below the English question, you get the same question in Hindi.

26
00:01:47,330 --> 00:01:53,110
The options need a square root, so open Maths & symbols. This is Sy Pad.

27
00:01:53,110 --> 00:01:57,170
Click option A, write the root, and press Insert.

28
00:01:57,170 --> 00:02:02,170
All four options are in. Now click the letter of the correct answer — D. That's it.

29
00:02:02,170 --> 00:02:04,770
One question, two languages.

30
00:02:05,570 --> 00:02:08,860
To add the second question, press Add question.

31
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:15,100
Small tip — a new question opens in the last language you used, so tap English first.

32
00:02:15,110 --> 00:02:20,060
This question has a diagram, and there's no need to redraw it.

33
00:02:20,050 --> 00:02:23,360
Click Picture, and choose the screen button.

34
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:31,220
Now, in the PDF, press Windows, Shift and S together, drag a box around the diagram, come back, and press Control V.

35
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:37,150
Look — the diagram sits under the question and above the options, exactly like the paper.

36
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:39,890
The fraction options come from Sy Pad.

37
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:41,470
Correct answer: B.

38
00:02:42,270 --> 00:02:47,400
Question three is chemistry, and here the structure sits right inside the sentence.

39
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:53,530
TestoZa doesn't have a structure-drawing tool, so we simply cut it from the paper.

40
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:56,650
In Picture, choose the cloud button.

41
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:59,860
It places the image exactly where your cursor is.

42
00:02:59,860 --> 00:03:05,090
Next to it, the reaction arrow from Sy Pad — ozone on top, zinc and water below.

43
00:03:05,090 --> 00:03:07,370
This one is numerical.

44
00:03:07,370 --> 00:03:14,200
Up in Question type, choose Numerical answer, click Exact value, and type the answer — one.

45
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,760
Now it's time for maths. Open Maths & symbols.

46
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:25,120
At the top it says "Goes into Question 4", so the formula lands in question four.

47
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:29,410
f of x equals the integral… inside, a fraction…

48
00:03:29,410 --> 00:03:31,670
x squared dx on top…

49
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:39,910
and two brackets below — one plus x squared in the first, and in the second, one plus the root of one plus x squared.

50
00:03:39,910 --> 00:03:42,070
Watch the preview at the top.

51
00:03:42,070 --> 00:03:47,820
As you type, the question builds up exactly like the paper.

52
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:51,920
Press Insert, and type the rest of the line.

53
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:55,570
The options use log, root and pi by four — all from Sy Pad.

54
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:59,200
The last option is plain text: None of these.

55
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:00,960
Correct answer: B.

56
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:07,790
And now, the biggest question in this video — a JEE-level multistep reaction.

57
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:13,420
First, the bromobenzene structure, with the cloud button, right at the cursor.

58
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:20,940
Then open Chemistry in Sy Pad, and pick the arrow with conditions above and below.

59
00:04:20,930 --> 00:04:26,510
Press plus on top to make three rows, and remove the bottom one.

60
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:27,340
Now the three sets of reagents.

61
00:04:27,330 --> 00:04:32,020
One: magnesium and ether, then carbon dioxide and H plus.

62
00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:37,350
Two: ammonia and heat. Three: bromine and sodium hydroxide.

63
00:04:37,350 --> 00:04:40,990
And this time, the options are structures too.

64
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,360
Use the picture button next to each option to add its image.

65
00:04:45,350 --> 00:04:50,060
Five diagrams in a single question, and it's still perfectly clean.

66
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:52,810
Correct answer: B — aniline.

67
00:04:53,610 --> 00:04:58,510
For a match-the-list question, you don't need to draw a table.

68
00:04:58,520 --> 00:05:01,370
In Sy Pad, open Tables and choose Match List.

69
00:05:01,370 --> 00:05:04,440
Reactants on the left, products on the right.

70
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:06,960
Fill in the boxes, and press Insert.

71
00:05:06,970 --> 00:05:08,500
Correct answer: C.

72
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:10,640
Our paper is ready.

73
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:16,860
Now let's split it into Physics, Chemistry and Mathematics, just like the real JEE.

74
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:22,580
First, grab the integral question by its handle, and drag it to the very bottom.

75
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:27,940
Turn on "Split into sections", and every question lands in Section A.

76
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:38,620
Click the plus between two questions, choose New question here, and add one more chemistry question — with the complex's formula from Sy Pad's chemistry keys.

77
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:46,350
At the bottom, press Add a new section, name it Bonus, and add a maths question to it.

78
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:51,080
Now let's split Section A in two.

79
00:05:51,070 --> 00:05:56,310
Where chemistry begins, click the plus, and choose Split section here.

80
00:05:56,310 --> 00:06:00,310
Name the first part Physics, and the new one Chemistry.

81
00:06:00,310 --> 00:06:07,150
The integral question is still sitting in Chemistry, so split that out too, and name it Mathematics.

82
00:06:07,150 --> 00:06:10,690
And finally, merge Bonus into Mathematics.

83
00:06:10,690 --> 00:06:14,020
Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics — just like JEE.

84
00:06:14,820 --> 00:06:18,810
Now click Save test. Your test is in My Tests.

85
00:06:18,810 --> 00:06:25,100
And this is exactly what your candidates will see — sections, Hindi, diagrams, maths…

86
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:25,960
everything.

87
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:31,330
So go ahead — make your first test today at testoza.com.

88
00:06:31,340 --> 00:06:33,830
If you liked this video, do subscribe.

89
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:35,020
See you in the next one!
